162
00:11:49,273 --> 00:11:52,283
The car went north up the
interstate in the dark.

163
00:11:52,682 --> 00:11:54,873
The other half of him had an opinion.

164
00:11:55,393 --> 00:11:56,797
She was right, though.

165
00:11:57,197 --> 00:11:59,167
Wesker turned his head.

166
00:11:59,567 --> 00:12:01,297
In the silence, the passenger.

167
00:12:01,817 --> 00:12:07,310
The senator. Her question was correct. There is no
one on this earth who can make you

168
00:12:07,330 --> 00:12:07,635
stop.

169
00:12:08,365 --> 00:12:12,902
(very cold) No. And in about nine years, when there
is a stadium in Pennsylvania with

170
00:12:12,922 --> 00:12:17,836
ninety thousand people in it shouting the name of this
company, I would like you to remember

171
00:12:17,856 --> 00:12:22,501
that on the ninth of April 2034 I stood in front of
the government of the United States

172
00:12:22,521 --> 00:12:26,254
and told them precisely that, on the record,
